# A template's asset store holds raw bytes under extension-less, content-addressed
# names. Git guesses text-vs-binary for those, and a wrong guess on a machine with
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites line endings inside a JPEG or an Ogg — the file
# still checks out, but its content hash no longer matches the name it is filed
# under and the asset silently fails to load. Say it outright instead.
*/content/assets/content/** binary
